ed exactly one fenced Python block\" - so nothing ran. Yet evidence shows pages 9-12 from earlier. Hmm, actually maybe they were read in a previous session before this conversation. The state has remaining_model_calls 26 and evidence_catalog total 19. So pages 9-12 were read earlier (probably by earlier turns not shown).\n\nSo the run_command for read_pdf creates evidence with page content exposed. Good. So reading pages via run_command will expose them.\n\nNow, I must be careful about request size. When I call read_pdf for pages 13-18, the stdout may be ~25k chars, plus prompt already large (~? the system prompt + state is big, maybe 15k). Hmm, that could exceed 32000. The current request includes several evidence blobs (pages 9,11,12 large ~7k+4k+1.3k) plus instructions. That's already large.\n\nActually the request bodies are counted for real API requests; the eval counts the agent's model requests. The evidence injection is part of it. So I need to keep pages small per request: maybe 3-4 pages.\n\nCurrent request size seems maybe ~25k already with those evidence. Careful. Next request: if I don't call get_evidence, those won't be re-pinned... Actually exposed evidence stays? \"exposed\": true persists, and content may be re-sent each request? That would be bad. Likely the system re-sends visible evidence until context trimming. Hmm.\n\nTo be safe, read 3-4 pages per request and keep notes.\n\nStrategy: For each batch, run read_pdf for 3-4 pages. The result stdout gets exposed. I then mentally read it and write notes later. But notes need to be saved from visible evidence — fine.\n\nI need to be efficient: 26 calls. Reading 40 pages at 4 pages = 10 calls. Then verification, final notes (5), write, pytest, finish ~ 6 calls. Total ~16. OK.\n\nBut also need to re-read key pages for quotes/answers. I know the answers roughly from knowledge of the paper:\n- Categories: reasoning, acting (tool use?), interacting. The paper's three categories: Reasoning, Acting, Interacting. Table 1 Reasoning, Table 3 Interaction, Acting... So categories: \"reasoning\", \"acting\", \"interacting\". Search methods: paper says \"we started with a keyword search ... then used snowballing\"? Need to verify. Likely \"keyword_search\" and \"snowballing\" (backward/forward snowballing).\n- Self Consistency: majority vote over multiple reasoning paths. ToT: depth-first search and breadth-first search controllers? The table says \"depth-first-search prompts\". Paper says ToT uses two search controllers: BFS and DFS.\n- Toolformer tools: calculator, question answering, machine translation, Wikipedia search, calendar. ToolBench: 16,464 APIs.\n- CAMEL: role-playing with \"inception prompting\". Generative Agents evaluators: 100? Need to check.\n- Table 4 topics: e.g., \"Reasoning\", \"Tool use\", \"Multi-agent\", \"Self-improvement/learning\", \"Safety\"? Need actual. Shared foundations: \"reasoning\" and ... maybe \"planning\" and \"memory\"? Actually \"all three capabilities benefit from ... reasoning and ...\"? Need read.\n\nLet me proceed reading pages 13-16 next. But I should be mindful of the huge evidence already present. Perhaps the past exposure won't be re-sent if I don't get_evidence them. But the state shows them \"recent\" — probably the runtime includes recent exposed evidence. The page 9,11,12 blobs are large. Next request might drop them.\n\nLet me just do it: run read_pdf 13-15 (3 pages) to check size.\n\nActually the tool call's stdout is returned; I see it in result. Let me do 13-16.\n\nCareful with byte counting: pages avg 4k chars, 4 pages=16k. Plus prompt. Risky. I'll do 3 pages first to gauge.\n\nAlso I should save overview note when I have content. But notes must be saved from visible evidence; page 1-2 content was in earlier turns (not in this request). ev-000005/8 page1 exposed earlier. In this request, pages 9,11,12 are visible. Page 10 not.\n\nOK proceed: read 9-10 too? Page 10 8k chars - large. Let me read page 10 alone next along